WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:06.660
Papa [Hamilton Johnston, professor in the College of Engineering] designed the stadium, and that was, that was even before we came over here.

2
00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:09.140
He was very provoked though two or three years later after it was built.

3
00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:17.980
They made him put rooms under all that, rooms to make, and he just thought that was a terrible idea.

4
00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:20.260
He said he had built it and it was all working very well,

5
00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:24.280
and to stick all these little, all these people in regular cells down underneath it.

6
00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:26.260
He just thought that was terrible, but he did it of course, there wasn’t any, and . . .

7
00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:35.580
Well that was during the Depression, and they wanted, they needed, this was when the expansion of the student population started . . .

8
00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:36.300
Right.

9
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:43.620
. . . and they needed some low-cost housing for men, and they sought, thought that since they had the structure there,

10
00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:49.240
they could build room, rooms much, at much lower cost than they could a new building, and of course they could.

11
00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:51.360
But they weren’t what you would call comfortable.

12
00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:55.747
They were more like cells [laughs], and I think they have been regarded as that since.
